{
  "dom_id": "step-q61861",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Nathan invested $\\$5\\,600$ into a company which then went on to lose $7%$ of its value every year. Which expression gives the value of Nathan's investment after $3$ years?",
  "worked_solution": "The number $7%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.07.$ Therefore, a decrease of $7%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.07=0.93\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{3}$ dollars.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
